WEBVTT

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.820
There were four Idaten present 
at the scene of the battle,

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:17.280
one of which we had no data on
and was exceptionally strong.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.650
She's also apparently a survivor
 from 800 years ago...

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.710
From before the demons were wiped out.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.420
I never would've guessed 
one of them was still alive.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.840
Is Nickel's transmitter still functioning? 
It was surgically implanted.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.880
The audio feed went dead not long 
after G-Thirteen was eliminated.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.850
I have to imagine someone noticed 
and intentionally disabled it.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.560
<i>You can implant it internally
 to keep it hidden,</i>

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.920
<i>but you can't expect me to miss 
the actual signal coming out of it.</i>

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:50.610
That means they knew all 
about the first transmitter

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:55.920
and left it partially functional 
in order to gauge our response!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.760
W-Wait, isn't this bad news?

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.990
If they attack us now...

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.650
B-B-Brandy-san, we're counting on you!

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.900
Wh-What are you talking about?!
 I telling you I can win, either! No way!

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.350
I think I still have a lot 
of growing to do, y'know?

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.550
Let's keep our expectations 
in check, shall we?

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:16.030
Oh, my! Are we all going to be slaughtered?

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:19.570
Oh, I've always wondered what it'd 
be like to be on the receiving end...

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:21.470
<b>Throb</b>

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:21.470
<b>Throb</b>

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:21.470
<b>Throb</b>

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:21.470
<b>Throb</b>

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:21.470
Why is this turning you on?!

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:22.840
Rabble, rabble, rabble...

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.440
Enough! Would you all shut your traps?!

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.480
<b><i>Hush</i></b>

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.480
Hush...

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.730
It's true enough that 
we can't win as things stand.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.650
Nevertheless, we can't just 
keep our heads down.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.640
If we ignore those three fledglings,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.120
they could grow to become 
monsters in their own right.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.660
Piscalat. Neput. Cory.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.020
The three of you will be responsible 
for exterminating them!

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.460
Use the military to find and track them.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.070
Human troops?

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:52.930
Exactly. They won't attack human soldiers.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:55.230
We've infiltrated human society 
in order to evade them...

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.840
We'll have to strike once they 
split up and are isolated.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.460
<i>Makes sense.</i>

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:01.940
<i>We use the humans for intelligence,</i>

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:04.710
<i>and when an opportunity 
presents itself, we attack.</i>

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:09.350
<i>That's the safest tactic, given that 
they're protecting the humans...</i>

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.860
I'll kill them all.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.410
If the demons are hiding in a human nation

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.360
and there's no way to tell the two apart,

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.610
then I'll blow the whole country off the map!

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:21.850
<i>It's impressive that she'd suggest the most 
brutal solution without any hesitation...</i>

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:25.100
<i>I bet even the demons would be surprised.</i>

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:39.080
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.000
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:04.010
<b>#4
Yellow Sparrow</b>

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:04.010
Ysley, tell me where this 
Zoble place is right now!

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.700
I'm going to wipe it out as soon as possible!

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.010
N-N-Now, let's take a second 
to calm down here, Rin-san!

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:13.100
We don't know how many demons there are,
or what kinds we're dealing with.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.850
To be on the safe side, 
why don't we try bringing in Prontea-san?

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:18.150
Bring in Prontea?

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.900
I admit he <i>would</i> be a great help,

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:27.450
but I entrusted him with 
monitoring the entire world.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.530
I wouldn't know where 
to start looking for him.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.870
Huh? But Prontea-san is—

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.060
Right?! So we'll go and search him out!

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.840
Could you wait a week before taking action?

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.800
What are you talking about, Ysley?

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.840
Prontea-san's going to be
 in Hotaena like always.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.590
I'll explain later!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.100
A week it is, then. Find Prontea and—

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.050
All right, Granny! I'm all healed up!

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.730
Let's get this training started already!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:55.660
I was talking, you fool!

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.290
That idiotic pupil of mine...

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:02.080
<i>He was able to land an attack 
on Rin-san by himself...</i>

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.130
<i>And he managed to budge her?</i>

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.700
Come on, you old fart! That all you got?!

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.570
Hurry up and bring it on!

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:14.090
What's gotten into him?

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.660
I'll have to shut him up the hard way...

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.030
<i>He's recovering at an incredible rate, too.</i>

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.470
<i>Our bodies are corporealized thought.</i>

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.950
<i>It's natural that our state of mind
 affects our physiology...</i>

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.020
<i>But it seems his loss, and the earnest 
hunger for strength that it inspired,</i>

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.840
<i>has powered him up a fair bit.</i>

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:35.740
Damn it, why are we watching 
some rinky-dink island?

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.060
Quit complaining.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.520
Are these three kids really 
worth all the trouble?

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.500
Check out the one with the pigtails, though.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.820
A little on the young side, 
but she's pretty cute!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:47.280
Hey, that's a nice rack! 
Wonder if we're allowed to mess her up...

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.710
<i>No one on these boats has noticed me.</i>

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:50.770
They said we're allowed to
 if we can pull this off.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:52.050
<i>They're all human.</i>

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.680
<i>But it's only been a half a day,</i>

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.080
<i>and now tens of thousands 
of troops are encircling the area...</i>

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:02.570
<i>When I was young, the world population 
numbered in the thousands.</i>

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.760
<i>There are almost too 
many humans at this point.</i>

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:08.590
<i>I could try to kill them all, 
but some are bound to get away...</i>

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:11.760
<i>It seems waiting for Prontea
 is the wise move after all.</i>

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.600
General Piscalat! It's that woman again.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:19.810
All of our naval troops' reports
 have been about her, too.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.900
<i>Why is she the only one? 
Have they already gone separate ways?</i>

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.830
Where does she keeping 
appearing from, though?

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:27.070
<i>For them to split up immediately 
after the battle with Nickel...</i>

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:29.000
She keeps popping in and 
out from seemingly nowhere.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:30.890
<i>Is this a trap to lure us in? 
Or something else?</i>

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:39.140
That's quite the armada. 
They responded faster than I thought.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:42.100
We'll head to Hotaena 
by traveling along the seafloor.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.390
Hey, why didn't you just 
call Prontea-san over?

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:47.990
Because if I did, he wouldn't show up.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:50.100
He's got an aversion to Rin-san.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:52.400
If she goes nuclear on Zoble right now,

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.430
it'll be hard to ensure 
all the demons are dead.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.130
There'd be no way to verify 
that we got them all.

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:59.350
Besides, it's a good idea to make sure

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.600
the two remaining superpowers won't start 
fighting as soon as Zoble is wiped out.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.310
But if we can clear those obstacles,

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:09.560
Rin-san and Prontea-san 
can take care of the rest.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.850
<i>While his general outlook was correct,</i>

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:15.160
<i>at the time, Ysley had no way of knowing</i>

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.500
<i>that his assumptions about the demon lord</i>

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.630
<i>were fundamentally off-base.</i>

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.650
General Piscalat! It's terrible!

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:26.380
We've discovered the body 
of Lieutenant G-Thirteen!

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:28.160
Oh, did you?

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.880
<i></i>That's<i> her response?</i>

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.090
Wait, something's not right here...

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:36.880
<i>Your Lordship, something 
has come to my attention.</i>

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:39.500
<i>What became of Gyudo
 the demon beast's body?</i>

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:43.330
Come to think of it, 
I wasn't able to retrieve it.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.830
<i>We just recovered G-Thirteen's,</i>

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:49.440
<i>but there's no sign of Nickel's.</i>

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:55.420
I'm just speculating, but what if 
the Idaten have already collected Gyudo?

00:07:55.420 --> 00:08:00.060
<i>You're suggesting that, wherever they took it,
they took Nickel to the same place?</i>

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.730
I would assume they mean to study
us demons in order to learn our secrets.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:09.600
I see. And since they would 
need humans to expedite the study...

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:12.980
That makes our destination
 Hotaena, doesn't it?

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.780
Goal!

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.630
<i>Damn, this dude's tall...</i>

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:41.950
I have to ask, new champ, 
what's the secret to your speed?

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:45.710
There's no need for special 
customization or hardware.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.900
For me, it all comes down 
to racing technique.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.410
I-I see...

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:53.390
Now, do you have any future goals?

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:54.720
I'm actually done with racing.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:55.550
Huh?

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:58.240
I got a result I'm satisfied with...

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.710
which means this experiment 
has come to an end.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:05.830
Hey, you again, Ysley-kun?

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:06.690
What's up?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.440
Paula and I just arrived at the Zeyo Coast.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.020
Oh, Paula's with you?

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.490
Okay, I'll be right there!

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:15.450
Huh? He's gone...

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.880
Good afternoon, Prontea-san.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.800
It's been so long, Prontea-san!

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.040
I really haven't seen you two in a while!

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.750
Idaten...

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:30.890
Fire!

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.550
How's my magic power, Ysley-kun?

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:42.890
I-It was pretty rude, for one thing.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:46.890
Was that the full intensity you can manifest?

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.000
Well, yeah!

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.430
It's hotter than any flamethrower, you'll find.

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:58.460
Although, it looks like you're 
not actually here for fun...

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:00.410
Let's hear the details.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:04.660
<i>The land of liberty, Hotaena.</i>

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.860
<i>Formed by the world's business interests,</i>

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:08.840
<i>it is a nation based 
on the idea of a free market.</i>

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.750
<i>For those with enough money,</i>

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:14.000
<i>it could be considered the most 
peaceful place in the world...</i>

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.940
Hey, it's the big guy!

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.260
Hey, hey! You've gotta tell us more tricks!

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.950
I'm a little busy today.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.760
You're really popular, Prontea-san.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.900
That's because he's amazing!

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:27.930
He can find tricks that aren't 
even in strategy guides!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.270
He's totally on god mode!

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.770
Tricks that aren't in strategy guides?

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:34.430
Does that mean you've 
figured out how to do it?

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:39.690
Well, yeah. I don't think it'll be as 
helpful as you imagined, though, Ysley-kun.

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:41.990
Hey, Paula. Where the hell are we?

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:46.120
Settle down, Hayato! This is a human town.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:49.210
What? What am I doing here?!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.950
And where's the old bag?!

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.930
Granny! Hey, Granny!

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.930
He's an Idaten?

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.430
You old bitch!

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:55.050
Is the head in the box, too?

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:56.510
Where the hell are you?!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.020
Well, I'll explain in due time...

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.040
What happened to training, huh?!

00:10:58.020 --> 00:10:59.990
Who's the granny he keeps yelling about?

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:03.430
Get your wrinkly ass out here, Granny!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.430
That's going to have to wait, too...

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:07.360
So they're somewhere in this country...

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:11.980
How are we supposed to find them, though? 
There are too many humans around.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:17.000
I wouldn't worry. The Demon Lord will 
be utilizing the humans to locate them.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.550
All we've gotta do is kill them.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:28.700
You've really changed 
this room up a lot, huh?

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:34.130
That's right. See, all of the footage from 
these monitors is linked directly to my mind.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:40.090
I've been making use of the potential Idaten 
abilities that Ysley-kun hypothesized.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:42.990
This magic works the same way.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:46.890
I sadly don't have the technical ability 
to experiment with my own theories.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:48.610
I'm grateful for your assistance.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:51.630
Hey, who gives a shit?!

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:54.860
We're here to drag this guy
 back to Granny, right?

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:57.530
Kind of a rude boy, isn't he?

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:59.120
Who's this "Granny," anyway?

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:03.160
Prontea-san, I need you to stay as 
calm as possible when I tell you this.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:08.790
The granny that Hayato 
is referring to... is Rin-san.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.390
<i>I saw this coming...</i>

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:18.850
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry, Master!

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:20.900
I'm sorry for playing video 
games at home all day!

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:24.880
But they're gone, you know?! 
There aren't any demons anywhere!

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:26.820
Wait, what?! 
You want me to bring them to you?!

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:29.770
Is this— Are you mad at me?!
 You are, aren't you?!

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.280
Game over, man! Game over!
She's gonna kill me!

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:35.010
Please don't kill me! I'm begging you!
 I'm begging for mercy!

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:39.270
It was all my fault!
I'm so sorry, so just spare my life!

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.560
Master!

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:45.170
Sorry, but we're going to have to 
give him time to calm down.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:46.790
And it might be a while...

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.280
What's this?

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.080
It's apparently footage from 
every camera in Hotaena.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:57.540
Everything from public security 
cameras to home video recorders.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.520
Is this that hacking thing?

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:03.640
How does that work for 
cameras that aren't online

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.940
or aren't connected to anything at all?

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:10.720
No clue. The Demon Lord's 
technology is beyond any of us.

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:16.730
So she's not mad? You promise?

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.930
Yes. It's okay.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:21.960
We've been given a week of 
free time under the pretense

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:24.190
of looking for you, Prontea-san.

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:25.950
I was hoping to get your help

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.580
performing a psychohack 
on Zoble's computer network

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:32.990
in order to help ensure our demon hunt's 
efficacy by verifying their numbers.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:37.760
That being said, since the task 
itself won't take very long...

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:41.750
How about it, Hayato? 
Care to train a bit with Prontea-san?

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.090
With this dude who's 
scared shitless of the old bag?

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.260
Is he actually strong?

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:51.270
You keep talking about her like that...
 Doesn't she scare you?

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:54.060
Like she's <i>not</i> gonna kick my ass
 as hard if I'm nice to her?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.980
You can be polite or you can talk shit,

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.020
either way, that psycho hag 
will mess you up all the same.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.030
Ysley-kun, how long has 
he been training with Master?

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:05.710
Eighty years.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:09.780
And his spirit has never once broken.
It's impressive.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:11.740
Anyway...

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:18.510
I need to start looking into this. 
I'll leave things here to you, Prontea-san.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.680
Okay, then, I believe 
your name is Hayato-kun?

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:27.220
We'll do your training first 
in lieu of an introduction.

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:29.280
You, too, Paula.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.600
<i>If Hayato and Prontea-san go head to head, 
the demons are bound to notice.</i>

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.800
<i>But they won't be able to beat Prontea-san.</i>

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:44.470
<i>If we can capture one of them alive, 
things should proceed smoothly from there.</i>

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.120
Emperor Takeshita.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.490
On monitor 2034...

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.370
could you rewind four seconds?

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.830
Oh, very well.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.070
Did you find them, Barcode?

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:59.440
Sorting large amounts of data 
is my specialty, after all.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.290
It's only for a second,

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:04.250
but I imagine you and the emperor 
will be able to see him, too.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:08.550
I see now. Looks like the first one 
will be the little boy in glasses.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:12.100
<i>Piscalat, you're assigned 
to deal with this one.</i>

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:13.300
Copy that.

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.860
Is this supposed to be your idea of fire?

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.010
You think that's gonna work on me?!

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.620
<i>What the hell? Ice?</i>

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:39.700
Self-Taught Explosion!

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.090
What's your deal?

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.810
You some kind of wizard or something?

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:54.920
And is that the best you've got?

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:57.760
Or are you screwing around 
with me and holding back?

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:00.480
Either way, it's pissing me off.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.900
I hit you as hard as I could!

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:06.120
It's just that I've only recently learned
 these magic-esque attacks, you see.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:09.940
<i>That was strong enough 
to beat Ysley-kun and Paula...</i>

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:13.200
<i>He's as rugged as I'd expect 
from training under Master.</i>

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.900
I haven't had much opportunity
for practical exercises...

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:21.450
so I appreciate your cooperation!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.050
I already told you that won't cut it!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.340
<i>Damn it, seriously?!</i>

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.440
<i>My attacks don't work on him, either?!</i>

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:39.930
<i>Ah, I see.</i>

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:49.590
Looks like it has an additive effect if 
I use it in combination with a normal attack.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:54.590
I understand why Ysley-kun 
brought you to see me now.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:58.450
Your strength is fundamentally 
lacking something, Hayato-kun.

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:01.160
Would you like me to teach you about it?

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:05.740
Suppose this creature was alive
 and needed to be killed.

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:07.570
How would you do it, Dr. Gachikama?

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.500
Well, let's see...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.010
I have to think that poison would be

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:16.470
the simplest approach, like you
 originally suggested, Ysley-chan.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:20.460
And if you were going to poison him, 
what would be the theoretical lethal dose?

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:24.460
Let's see... Tetrodotoxin seems to work,

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:28.260
so if we fed him 50,000 pufferfish,
 maybe that would kill him.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.480
I'm not sure I'd describe that as "simple."

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:35.240
Even military-grade chemical weapons 
would take more than half an hour.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.630
Now, I've compiled the results of 
our research for you like usual,

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:40.870
so be sure to take these with you.

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:42.010
Here.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:47.040
Well, knowing that poison is effective 
at all is pretty convenient.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:49.630
Continue your research, Doctor.

00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:55.880
Did you know another doctor named 
Obami during your time in Zoble?

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:57.440
Obami?

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.610
Oh, you couldn't <i>not</i> know him.

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:03.990
Zoble didn't care about research 
unless that old guy was running it!

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:07.440
It was always something to do with 
cloning some sort of strange organism

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.350
and in vitro fertilization...

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:16.560
<i>I see. So the demons are trying
 to find a way to propagate.</i>

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.010
Ysley-sama! There's trouble!

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.660
Did something happen in this storeroom?

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:37.590
You'll... You'll spare my life now, right?

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:47.920
You might be weaker than the rest, 
but you're still an Idaten, I see.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:52.030
If nothing else, you're quick on your feet.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:54.790
But you're trapped like a rat in here,

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:58.020
so why don't we have a little fun?

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:01.030
<i>That's Piscalat, one of Zoble's generals!</i>

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.160
My ambush might not have worked,

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:06.910
but I have to wonder how long you'll be 
able to evade me in a room like this.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:17.590
Damn, I can't see a thing.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.460
<i>Can he see in the dark?</i>

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:37.340
<i>But as it stands, 
I can't risk making a move...</i>

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:38.400
<i>That's a relief.</i>

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:43.210
<i>The next question is if I can avoid 
an attack from the entrance...</i>

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:49.500
<i>It'll be a problem if I can't 
land an attack from this range.</i>

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.940
<i>This might be harder than I anticipated.</i>

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:01.220
What the hell? Did you start pulling 
your punches all of a sudden?

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:04.470
Get serious, damn it!
 That doesn't hurt at all!

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.240
It doesn't?

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:10.140
But I was hitting about as 
hard as you do, Hayato-kun.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.150
S-Say what?

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:14.900
That's your weakness. Basically—

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.850
Did that smash them all?

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:25.050
Man, how dumb are these guys if we could
find them without the Demon Lord's help?

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:30.690
Well, it looks like the demons managed 
to track down all the commotion...

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:33.530
I suppose your lesson will have 
to wait until we take care of them.

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:35.000
Okay, Hayato-kun?

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:37.000
Y-Yeah...

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:41.340
<i>Damn, this guy's a freak of nature, too.</i>

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.180
What the—?!

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:53.980
Too weak!

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:59.370
<i>It seems magic doesn't 
work on demons, either.</i>

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:01.060
<i>This one is strong.</i>

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:02.820
<i>But this one...</i>

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:03.650
Hup!

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:13.890
Paula, Hayato-kun! You two take
 that one. Go ahead and beat him.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:16.660
Ow...

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:20.300
Now that the matchups are decided...

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:19.040
<b>CORY</b>

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:19.040
<b>HAYATO & PAULA</b>

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:21.550
<b>PRONTEA</b>

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:21.550
<b>NEPUT</b>

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:23.300
Let's get it on, shall we?

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.050
<b>YSLEY</b>

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.050
<b>PISCALAT</b>
